  "body": "Another issue found when changing summary element to use \"display: list-item\" in [Bug 1258657](https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1258657) for Firefox.\n\nThat is, `<li>` inside `<summary>` inherits `list-style-position: inside` from `<summary>` per spec in [14.5.3 The details and summary elements](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/rendering.html#the-details-and-summary-elements)\n\nFor example, the `<li>First item</li>` will have `list-style-position: inside`.\n\n``` html\n<details >\n  <summary>Summary\n    <ul>\n      <li>First item</li>\n    </ul>\n  </summary>\n</detalis>\n```\n\nWe might need to add something like the following to compensate the inheritance.\n\n``` css\nsummary ol, summary ul, summary menu {\n  list-style-position: initial;\n}\n```\n\ncc @tabatkins @annevk @upsuper @bzbarsky \n",
